# A host's answers are the next tick's input (ruling HO, Language ch. 6, "Tick by tick":
# "no prompt cycle runs through a host: hosting means inserting delay"): `@Boxed` hosts
# its child, handing each place the box's own clicks, `!in`, and the box element reads the
# places, `$elems`; `!in` is prompt on `$elems`, but nothing the handler captures is an edge
# of the host's line, so there is no cycle. Found by the step 3 build on chess (`@Grid`,
# `@VBox`, ...) and on the library (`@HostDocument`'s `$guests` and `Supply`).
# Written by Claude on the claude-self-hosting branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.* | Box.*

family Box

tag Box.Click of Element !unit:
    label: Text

tag Box.Frame of Element !Path:
    $children: (Path ==> $Elem)

?Answered: fn Path, Element o, !Path -> ?@o
fn ?Answered p, e, !in = match e:
    Box.Click(..): ? @ (unit on !in)
    otherwise: nil

@Boxed: fn prompt @a -> @a
fn @Boxed @child:
    ((r, $elems)) <- @HostSome @child, \|p, e| ?Answered p, e, !in
    !in <- Box.Frame($children=$elems)
    @ r
